oTableGrid\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes;\">\n<td style=\"width: 468.0pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #D6EAF8; padding: 7.0pt 10.0pt 7.0pt 10.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"624\">\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #1f4e79;\">💡<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>Debug Tips: Enable Terraform debug logging with:<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>export TF_LOG=DEBUG &amp;&amp; terraform apply<br>Enable Ansible verbose output with:<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>ansible-playbook -vvv playbook.yml</span></em></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Cambria\',serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: \'MS Mincho\'; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h1 style=\"margin: 12.0pt 0cm 6.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; color: #1f4e79;\">Appendix A: Installation Guide</span></h1>\n<h2 style=\"margin: 12.0pt 0cm 6.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 13.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; color: #2e75b6;\">A.1 Install Terraform on Ubuntu/Debian</span></h2>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">curl -fsSL https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com/gpg | \\</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/hashicorp-archive-keyring.gpg</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">echo \"deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/hashicorp-archive-keyring.gpg] \\</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | \\</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/hashicorp.list</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install terraform -y</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">terraform version</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 4.0pt 0cm 4.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h2 style=\"margin: 12.0pt 0cm 6.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 13.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; color: #2e75b6;\">A.2 Install Ansible and Cloud Collections</span></h2>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"># Install Python and Ansible</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">pip3 install ansible boto3 botocore oci</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">ansible --version</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"># Install cloud provider collections</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">ansible-galaxy collection install amazon.aws</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">ansible-galaxy collection install oracle.oci</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">ansible-galaxy collection install community.general</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 4.0pt 0cm 4.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h2 style=\"margin: 12.0pt 0cm 6.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 13.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; color: #2e75b6;\">A.3 Install OCI CLI</span></h2>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">bash -c \"$(curl -L https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oracle/oci-cli/master/scripts/install/install.sh)\"</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"># Configure (follow prompts for tenancy, region, key)</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">oci setup config</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\"># Test connectivity</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background: #1E1E1E; margin: 0cm 18.0pt 0cm 18.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Courier New\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #d4d4d4;\">oci iam region list</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 4.0pt 0cm 4.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 4.0pt 0cm 4.0pt 0cm;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>','2026-06-15 06:23:47','Infrastucture Management',NULL,0,0),
(184,'AI Systems & Architecture','ai-systems-architechture','<header>\n<h1>&nbsp;AI Systems &amp; Architecture</h1>\n<p>A Complete Engineer\'s Guide to LLM, RAG, AI Agents, MCP, Agentic AI, and LLM Cost Optimization &mdash; from fundamentals to production architecture.</p>\n<div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"badge\">📅 June 2026</span><span class=\"badge\">🎯 Beginner to Advanced</span><span class=\"badge\">⏱ 25 min read</span><span class=\"badge\">🏷 AI &middot; Architecture &middot; DevOps</span></div>\n</header><nav>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#intro\">Introduction</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#ai-analogy\">AI Analogy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#llm-rag-agents\">LLM, RAG &amp; Agents</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#mcp\">MCP Protocol</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#mcp-vs-rag\">MCP vs RAG vs Skills</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#agentic-arch\">Agentic Architecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#context-eng\">Context Engineering</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#cost-opt\">Cost Optimization</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#event-driven\">Event-Driven AI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#terminology\">Terminology</a></li>\n</ul>\n</nav><main>\n<div class=\"toc\">\n<h2>📋 Table of Contents</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#intro\">Introduction to Modern AI Systems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#ai-analogy\">Understanding AI Using a Human Analogy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#llm-rag-agents\">LLM, RAG, and AI Agents Explained</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#mcp\">What is MCP? (Model Context Protocol)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#mcp-vs-rag\">MCP vs RAG vs Agent Skills &mdash; Architecture Comparison</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#agentic-arch\">Context Engineering for Agentic AI Systems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#cost-opt\">15 LLM Cost Optimization Techniques</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#event-driven\">Event-Driven Agentic AI Architecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.claudeusercontent.com/?domain=claude.ai&amp;parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai&amp;errorReportingMode=parent&amp;formattedSpreadsheets=true&amp;routeHandlerPdf=true#terminology\">6 Must-Know AI Agent Terminologies</a></li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n<section id=\"intro\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">1. Introduction to Modern AI Systems</h2>\n<div class=\"intro-box\">\n<p>AI is rapidly evolving from simple chatbots to autonomous systems capable of reasoning, planning, and taking actions across enterprise workflows. Understanding the architecture behind these systems is now as essential as understanding databases, APIs, or cloud infrastructure.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Most engineers encounter terms like&nbsp;<strong>LLM, RAG, AI Agents, and MCP</strong>&nbsp;as buzzwords &mdash; but without understanding the underlying architecture, it is hard to build production-grade systems. This guide breaks everything down from first principles, using simple human analogies and real-world examples.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-box blue\">\n<h4>💡 Why This Matters for Infrastructure Engineers</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>AI workloads are increasingly deployed on GPU clusters (H100, A100) and cloud infrastructure</li>\n<li>AI Agents interact with external APIs, databases, and file systems &mdash; exactly what DevOps manages</li>\n<li>Cost optimization of AI systems requires understanding token economics and caching strategies</li>\n<li>Agentic AI architectures involve Kafka, message queues, and event-driven patterns familiar to backend engineers</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section id=\"ai-analogy\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">2. Understanding AI Using a Human Analogy</h2>\n<p>The best way to understand the AI ecosystem is through a simple human analogy. Each component of a modern AI system maps to a human capability:</p>\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🧠&nbsp;LLM = Brain</strong></div>\n<p>A Large Language Model is the reasoning engine. It learns patterns from massive data, understands language, and generates intelligent responses. It can think &mdash; but cannot automatically access the latest information.</p>\n<span class=\"tag\">claude-sonnet, gpt-4, gemini</span></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>📚&nbsp;RAG = Brain + Books</strong></div>\n<p>Retrieval-Augmented Generation allows the AI to search documents, databases, websites, and PDFs before answering. Instead of relying only on trained knowledge, it fetches up-to-date information in real time.</p>\n<span class=\"tag\">vector db + llm</span></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🤲&nbsp;AI Agent = Brain + Hands</strong></div>\n<p>An AI Agent doesn\'t just answer &mdash; it acts. It can send emails, schedule meetings, update CRMs, create reports, trigger workflows, and manage customer support tasks autonomously.</p>\n<span class=\"tag\"><strong>tool_use + reasoning</strong></span></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🔌&nbsp;MCP = Connection Layer</strong></div>\n<p>Model Context Protocol is the standardized connector that lets AI systems communicate with the tools they need &mdash; files, APIs, databases, services &mdash; without custom integrations for every service.</p>\n<span class=\"tag\">protocol standard </span>LLM <small>Thinks </small>&rarr; RAG&nbsp; <small>Retrieves </small>&rarr; AI Agent <small>Acts </small>&rarr; MCP <small>Connects </small>&rarr; External Systems <small>APIs, DBs, Files</small></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"highlight-box green\">\n<h4>✅ Key Insight</h4>\n<p>Organizations that understand this shift &mdash; from chatbots to complete AI systems &mdash; will have a significant competitive advantage over the next decade. The future belongs to organizations that build complete AI systems where knowledge can be retrieved, actions can be executed, and systems can be connected.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section id=\"llm-rag-agents\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">3. LLM, RAG, and AI Agents Explained</h2>\n<h3>3.1 Large Language Models (LLM)</h3>\n<p>An LLM is a neural network trained on billions of text tokens from the internet, books, and code repositories. It learns statistical relationships between words and can generate coherent, contextually appropriate text.</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Characteristic</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Training Data</td>\n<td>Trillions of tokens from diverse sources</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Context Window</td>\n<td>4K &ndash; 200K tokens depending on model</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Knowledge Cutoff</td>\n<td>Fixed date &mdash; does not know recent events</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Strengths</td>\n<td>Reasoning, summarization, code generation, language understanding</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Limitations</td>\n<td>Hallucination, stale knowledge, no real-time access</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>3.2 Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)</h3>\n<p>RAG solves the LLM\'s knowledge cutoff problem by connecting it to live data sources. Here is how the RAG pipeline works step by step:</p>\n<div class=\"layer-diagram\">\n<div class=\"layer layer-1\">Step 1: User submits a query</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-2\">Step 2: Query is converted to an embedding vector</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-3\">Step 3: Vector database performs similarity search against stored document embeddings</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-4\">Step 4: Relevant chunks are retrieved and injected into the LLM prompt as context</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-5\">Step 5: LLM generates an answer grounded in the retrieved information</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"highlight-box yellow\">\n<h4>⚡ RAG Use Cases in Enterprise</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Internal knowledge base Q&amp;A (HR policies, runbooks, SOPs)</li>\n<li>Customer support bots that answer from live product documentation</li>\n<li>Legal document analysis and contract review</li>\n<li>Real-time monitoring alert summarization from log databases</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>3.3 AI Agents</h3>\n<p>An AI Agent is a system where the LLM is given&nbsp;<strong>tools</strong>&nbsp;it can call autonomously. Instead of just producing text, the agent can take actions in the world.</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Agent Capability</th>\n<th>Real-World Example</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Send emails</td>\n<td>Automatically notify stakeholders when a deployment fails</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Update CRM</td>\n<td>Log customer interactions without human input</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Query databases</td>\n<td>Fetch live metrics to answer \"how is my server performing?\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trigger workflows</td>\n<td>Create Jira tickets from monitoring alerts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Execute code</td>\n<td>Run diagnostic scripts and return results</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Manage files</td>\n<td>Read, write, and organize files on a file system</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"mcp\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">4. What is MCP? (Model Context Protocol)</h2>\n<div class=\"intro-box\">\n<p>MCP &mdash; Model Context Protocol &mdash; is an open standard developed to solve a critical problem: how do AI systems communicate with external tools and services in a consistent, secure, and reusable way?</p>\n</div>\n<p>Before MCP, every AI application needed custom integration code for every service. MCP provides a universal connector &mdash; like USB-C for AI systems.</p>\n<h3>MCP Architecture</h3>\n<div class=\"arch-flow\">\n<div class=\"flow-box\">User Query&nbsp; &rarr; MCP Client <small>(in the LLM app) </small>&harr; MCP Server <small>(hosted service) </small>&rarr; External Tools <small>Slack, Brave, Qdrant</small></div>\n</div>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Component</th>\n<th>Role</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MCP Client</td>\n<td>The AI host that sends requests</td>\n<td>Claude Desktop, cursor, custom app</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MCP Server</td>\n<td>Exposes tool capabilities over the protocol</td>\n<td>GitHub MCP, Slack MCP, File System MCP</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tool Registry</td>\n<td>Catalog of available tools the agent can discover</td>\n<td>List of functions with schemas</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protocol Transport</td>\n<td>Communication channel</td>\n<td>SSE (Server-Sent Events), stdio</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"highlight-box green\">\n<h4>✅ Benefits of MCP</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Write tool integration once &mdash; any MCP-compatible AI can use it</li>\n<li>Security and access control handled at the server layer</li>\n<li>Enables multi-agent systems to share the same tool ecosystem</li>\n<li>Open standard &mdash; not vendor-locked to any single AI provider</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section id=\"mcp-vs-rag\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">5. MCP vs RAG vs Agent Skills &mdash; Architecture Comparison</h2>\n<p>These three patterns are often confused. Here is a clear comparison of when to use each:</p>\n<div class=\"comparison-grid\">\n<div class=\"comp-card\">\n<h4>🔌 MCP (Model Context Protocol)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Protocol for connecting AI to external tools and services</li>\n<li>Enables real-time, bidirectional communication</li>\n<li>Handles tool discovery, execution, and response</li>\n<li>Best for: action-taking (send email, create ticket)</li>\n<li>Server-side tool management</li>\n<li>Security and auth at protocol level</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"comp-card\">\n<h4>📖 RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Pattern for grounding LLM in external knowledge</li>\n<li>Uses vector embeddings and similarity search</li>\n<li>Retrieves relevant document chunks at query time</li>\n<li>Best for: knowledge Q&amp;A and document search</li>\n<li>Vector DB + embedding model required</li>\n<li>Read-only &mdash; does not take actions</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"comp-card\">\n<h4>🛠 Agent Skills</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Reusable capabilities or actions specific to agent tasks</li>\n<li>Examples: Web search, code execution, email sending</li>\n<li>Managed by a Skill Manager within the Agent Host</li>\n<li>Best for: task-specific, repeatable agent behaviors</li>\n<li>Tied to the agent runtime</li>\n<li>Can combine RAG + MCP under one skill</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Dimension</th>\n<th>MCP</th>\n<th>RAG</th>\n<th>Skills</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Primary Use</td>\n<td>Tool connectivity</td>\n<td>Knowledge retrieval</td>\n<td>Task execution</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Data Flow</td>\n<td>Bidirectional</td>\n<td>Read-only</td>\n<td>Both</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Infrastructure</td>\n<td>MCP Server</td>\n<td>Vector DB</td>\n<td>Agent Host</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Latency</td>\n<td>Real-time</td>\n<td>Near real-time</td>\n<td>Task-dependent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cost Driver</td>\n<td>API calls</td>\n<td>Embedding + search</td>\n<td>Compute + LLM</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"agentic-arch\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">6. Context Engineering for Agentic AI Systems</h2>\n<p>Context Engineering is the practice of designing how information flows into and around an AI agent to make it reliable, accurate, and cost-efficient in enterprise settings.</p>\n<h3>Architecture Layers</h3>\n<div class=\"layer-diagram\">\n<div class=\"layer layer-1\">Layer 1: Inputs / Triggers &mdash; User Prompt, Kafka Events, API Triggers, Alert/Log, Workflow State Change</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-2\">Layer 2: Context Enrichment &mdash; Event Normalizer, Workflow State Lookup, Business Rules, Policy Context, User/Session Context</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-3\">Layer 3: Agent Orchestrator &mdash; Task Planner, Reasoning Engine, Confidence Check, Action Decision, Escalation Decision</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-4\">Layer 4: Knowledge &amp; Memory &mdash; RAG Pipeline, Vector Database, Knowledge Base, Short-Term Memory, Long-Term Memory</div>\n<div class=\"layer layer-5\">Layer 5: Tool Access &mdash; MCP Layer, Tool Registry, Agent Gateway, Approved APIs, SaaS Tools</div>\n</div>\n<h3>Actions / Outcomes</h3>\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>⚡&nbsp;API Action</strong></div>\n<p>Call external REST or GraphQL APIs to trigger business actions like creating orders or updating records.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🎫&nbsp;Ticket Update</strong></div>\n<p>Automatically create or update tickets in Jira, ServiceNow, or similar ITSM platforms.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>📊&nbsp;Report Generation</strong></div>\n<p>Generate structured reports, summaries, or dashboards from gathered data.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🔔&nbsp;Notification</strong></div>\n<p>Send alerts via Slack, email, PagerDuty, or SMS based on agent decisions.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h3>Governance &amp; Observability</h3>\n<div class=\"highlight-box blue\">\n<h4>🛡 Production AI Governance Requirements</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Guardrails:</strong>&nbsp;Input/output validation to prevent harmful or off-topic responses</li>\n<li><strong>PII Detection:</strong>&nbsp;Automatically detect and mask personally identifiable information</li>\n<li><strong>Audit Logs:</strong>&nbsp;Full trace of every agent decision, tool call, and output</li>\n<li><strong>Human-in-the-loop:</strong>&nbsp;Escalation paths for low-confidence or high-risk decisions</li>\n<li><strong>Tracing:</strong>&nbsp;Distributed tracing across all agent components (OpenTelemetry compatible)</li>\n<li><strong>Model Evaluation:</strong>&nbsp;Continuous evaluation of agent response quality</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section id=\"cost-opt\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">7. 15 LLM Cost Optimization Techniques</h2>\n<p>Running LLMs in production at scale can be expensive. Here are 15 proven techniques to reduce AI costs while maintaining performance:</p>\n<div class=\"techniques-grid\">\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>1&nbsp;Use Smaller Models</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Route simple queries to cheaper, faster models. Reserve large models for complex reasoning tasks only.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>2&nbsp;Multi-Model Routing</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Classify query complexity and route to the most appropriate model automatically based on difficulty.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>3&nbsp;Context Trimming</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Remove unnecessary or irrelevant conversation history before sending to the model to reduce input tokens.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>4&nbsp;Conversation Summarization</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Summarize long chat histories into compact memory instead of sending full conversation context each time.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>5&nbsp;Output Token Limits</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Set strict max_tokens limits on responses to prevent unnecessarily verbose outputs from the model.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>6&nbsp;RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Retrieve only the relevant information needed for a query rather than embedding entire document corpora in the prompt.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>7&nbsp;Response Caching</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Cache responses for repeated or similar queries. A cache hit costs zero tokens and returns instantly.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>8&nbsp;Prompt Caching</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Cache reusable system prompts or instructions so they are not re-processed on every API call.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>9&nbsp;Semantic Caching</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Use embeddings to match semantically similar queries to cached responses &mdash; not just exact string matches.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>10&nbsp;Structured Outputs</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Use JSON/XML output formats to reduce token waste from verbose free-text responses and ease parsing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>11&nbsp;Batch Processing</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Group multiple requests into batch jobs instead of individual API calls to leverage batch pricing discounts.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>12&nbsp;Agent Guardrails</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Add max tool call limits and timeouts to prevent runaway agent loops from consuming unlimited tokens.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>13&nbsp;Tool-First Architecture</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Use deterministic tools and APIs first; call the LLM only when reasoning is genuinely required.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>14&nbsp;Query Classification</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Classify incoming queries as FAQ, RAG, Agent, or Code tasks to route to the cheapest appropriate pipeline.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tech-item\">\n<div class=\"num\"><strong>15&nbsp;Cost Monitoring Dashboards</strong></div>\n<div>\n<p>Continuously monitor token usage, cost trends, and set budget alerts to catch runaway spending early.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"highlight-box green\">\n<h4>💰 Key Takeaway &mdash; Where the Biggest Savings Come From</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Smart Model Routing</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; can reduce costs by 60-80% by avoiding flagship models for simple tasks</li>\n<li><strong>Context Optimization</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; trimming and summarization typically saves 30-50% of input tokens</li>\n<li><strong>Effective RAG Implementation</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; avoids loading entire documents into context</li>\n<li><strong>Caching Strategies</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; semantic + response caching can eliminate 40-70% of repeat API calls</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section id=\"event-driven\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">8. Event-Driven Agentic AI Architecture</h2>\n<div class=\"intro-box\">\n<p>Enterprise AI should not only wait for a user prompt. In real business systems, many things happen automatically &mdash; Kafka events, API triggers, alerts, database changes, approval updates, and workflow state changes. This is why event-driven AI agents are becoming critical.</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Architecture Components</h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>Components</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Event Ingestion</td>\n<td>Kafka/MSK, API Gateway, Webhooks, EventBridge, Message Queue, DLQ</td>\n<td>Capture events from all sources reliably</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AI Orchestration</td>\n<td>Agent Orchestrator, Event Router, Task Planner, Workflow State Manager, Retry Handler</td>\n<td>Coordinate agent responses to events</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-Agent Runtime</td>\n<td>Triage Agent, Research/RAG Agent, Action Agent, Validation Agent, Notification Agent, Code Execution Agent</td>\n<td>Specialized agents handle different event types</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Agent Communication</td>\n<td>A2A Protocol Layer, Shared Context Bus</td>\n<td>Agents coordinate and share context</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tool Access</td>\n<td>MCP Layer, Tool Registry, Tool Adapters, Standardized Tool Interfaces</td>\n<td>Connect agents to external systems</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Agent Gateway</td>\n<td>Auth/N, Auth/Z, Rate Limiting, Policy Enforcement, Audit Logging, Network Egress Control</td>\n<td>Security and governance for outbound calls</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Memory Architecture in Agentic Systems</h3>\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>💬&nbsp;Short-Term Memory</strong></div>\n<p>Conversation and session context. Holds the current task state and recent exchanges. Cleared between sessions.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🗄&nbsp;Long-Term Memory</strong></div>\n<p>User, organization, and domain knowledge that persists across sessions. Stored in vector DBs or graph databases.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>🔍&nbsp;Semantic Cache</strong></div>\n<p>Prompt cache, embedding cache, and LLM response cache to avoid redundant computation across agents.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\"><strong>📂 Knowledge Base</strong></div>\n<p>Documents, wikis, policies, SOPs, and structured data accessible via RAG pipeline to all agents.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section id=\"terminology\">\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">9. 6 Must-Know AI Agent Terminologies</h2>\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\">🔌&nbsp;1. Model Context Protocol (MCP)</div>\n<p>A standard that lets AI agents connect to external tools, data sources, and services. Enables tools and agents to be interoperable across different AI platforms without custom integration.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\">🤖&nbsp;2. Single-Agent Architecture</div>\n<p>One AI agent perceives, decides, and acts on tasks using a fixed set of tools. Simple and easy to build, but limited in scope. Suitable for well-defined, bounded tasks.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\">🛠&nbsp;3. Skills &amp; Tool Usage</div>\n<p>Reusable capabilities assigned to agents &mdash; web search, code execution, email sending. Skills improve accuracy and efficiency for specific task types by combining LLM with deterministic logic.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\">👥&nbsp;4. Multi-Agent Architecture</div>\n<p>A system where multiple specialized agents collaborate by delegating tasks. A Manager Agent coordinates Specialist Agents (Research, Analysis, Execution). Better for complex, long-horizon tasks.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\">📖&nbsp;5. Agentic RAG</div>\n<p>AI agent that fetches, retrieves, and reasons over information dynamically during task execution. Goes beyond static RAG &mdash; the agent decides what to retrieve and when, iterating as needed.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"icon\">🧩 6. Memory Management</div>\n<p>How agents store and recall information &mdash; short-term (session), long-term (cross-session), episodic (past interactions), and semantic (factual knowledge). Critical for continuity and personalization.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"highlight-box red\">\n<h4>🚀 The Bottom Line</h4>\n<p>The shift from simple chatbots to autonomous AI agents is changing how software is designed, developed, and deployed. Organizations that build complete AI systems &mdash; where knowledge can be retrieved, actions can be executed, and systems can be connected &mdash; will have a decisive competitive advantage over the next 2&ndash;3 years. Understanding these six building blocks is as foundational as understanding APIs, databases, and cloud architecture.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n</main><footer>\n<p>✍️ Written by&nbsp;<strong>Krishnakumar</strong>&nbsp;| Senior Infrastructure &amp; Engineering Leader | Chennai, India</p>\n<p>Topics: AI Architecture &middot; LLM &middot; RAG &middot; Agents &middot; MCP &middot; Context Engineering &middot; Cost Optimization</p>\n</footer>','2026-06-15 13:08:14','AI',NULL,0,0),
